# Line endings.
#
# Every text blob in this repo is already stored with LF. That was luck — it
# held only while everyone's core.autocrlf happened to behave. On a Windows
# clone (autocrlf=true, the default) files check out as CRLF, and a commit made
# from certain editors or scripts can push those CRLF bytes back into the blob,
# which shows up as a whole-file rewrite in the diff.
#
# text=auto  — treat any file git detects as text as text
# eol=lf     — and give it LF both in the repo and in the working tree
#
# This is what let three source-matching regexes in extension/test.mjs fail on
# Windows only: content.js was checked out CRLF, so `;\r\n  }` never matched a
# pattern written as `;\n  }`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never inspected for line endings, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
